{0 Production policy}

Production behavior is selected once in {!module:Observe.Config}. Logging sites
remain ordinary point or wide authoring.

{1 Pipeline}

One completed log moves through these distinct decisions:

1. level and active-route admission;
2. caller authoring and configured enrichment;
3. finite materialization into package-owned meaning;
4. global caller-defined redaction;
5. one final sampling and retention decision;
6. per-drain routing and optional stricter redaction;
7. prompt acceptance or rejection by each selected drain; and
8. output-owned bounded delivery, flush, and shutdown.

Filtering is not sampling. Retention is not routing. Drain acceptance is not
delivery. Canonical safety is the shared floor, while a destination may choose
a stricter immutable projection.

{1 Enrichment}

{[
let deployment =
  Observe.Logs.Enricher.create_exn ~name:"deployment" (fun () ->
    Observe.Value.object_
      [ "region", Observe.Value.string "eu-west-1"
      ; "revision", Observe.Value.string release_revision
      ])
]}

The callback is lazy and runs only for an admitted completed log. It must
return an object contribution. Caller-authored fields win ordinary collisions.
[~authoritative_fields] grants one enricher authority over named non-reserved
root fields; configuration rejects overlapping authority, so list order never
selects a winner.

Callbacks are synchronous and may run concurrently for different logs. Ordinary
exceptions are contained and omit only that contribution; runtime control
exceptions remain native. A callback that recursively emits Observe logs owns
termination of that recursion.

{1 Finite materialization}

Finite defaults always apply. Select tighter workload-specific bounds when
needed:

{[
let limits =
  Observe.Logs.Limits.create_exn
    ~max_depth:16
    ~max_object_fields:128
    ~max_collection_length:256
    ~max_string_bytes:16_384
    ~max_bytes_length:16_384
    ~max_nodes:4_096
    ~max_total_bytes:262_144
    ()
]}

Limits apply to typed and open point and wide values, nested structures,
embedded typed values, recursion, strings, bytes, annotations, and required log
metadata. Local exhaustion preserves a safe prefix or sibling and records
package-owned truncation. Observe withholds the whole log only when it cannot
isolate the invalid region or guarantee the disclosure boundary.

[max_total_bytes] is deterministic Observe accounting, not an OCaml heap or wire
size. See {!val:Observe.Logs.Limits.create} for the stable charged units.

{1 Explicit redaction}

Observe supplies mechanics; the application supplies meaning. There are no
built-in PII, payment, credential, email, token, regex, or field-name presets.

{[
module R = Observe.Logs.Redaction

let disclosure =
  R.create_exn
    ~rules:
      [ R.Rule.at
          (R.Path.fields [ "customer"; "email" ])
          (R.Action.mask
             (R.Mask.keep_suffix ~characters:3
                ~hidden:(R.Mask.Collapse "***") ()))
      ; R.Rule.at
          (R.Path.fields [ "payment"; "access_token" ])
          R.Action.remove
      ]
    ()
]}

Exact paths can address fields, list indexes, and variant cases. Matching rules
can replace or mask matching structured scalars, point-text messages, and wide
annotations. A schema-associated policy validates known typed paths when it is
constructed.

The global policy runs before capture and every output. Failure is local and
fail-closed: an affected unsafe branch is replaced, removed, or withheld rather
than delivering the original. Redaction does not rewrite package metadata.

{1 Sampling and completion-aware retention}

{[
module S = Observe.Logs.Sampling

let sampling =
  S.create
    ~debug:(S.Rate.percent_exn 5.)
    ~info:(S.Rate.percent_exn 25.)
    ~stability:S.Correlation_stable
    ()

let retention =
  Observe.Logs.Retention.create ~keep:(fun log ->
    Observe.Level.equal (Observe.Log.level log) Observe.Level.Error)
]}

Omitted sampling is inert. Omitted per-level rates retain all logs, so errors
remain retained unless [~error] is explicitly configured. Exact zero and 100%
consume no random draw.

[Correlation_stable] aligns the base draw for related observations but does not
make a causal tree one buffered unit. Each point, parent, and child completes and
is retained independently.

Retention sees the completed bounded globally redacted {!type:Observe.Log.t}.
Returning [true] rescues it from base sampling; [false] defers to the base
decision and cannot force a drop. Failures are diagnosed and fail open.

{1 Routing and stricter destinations}

{[
let incidents =
  incident_drain
  |> Observe.Drain.with_route ~when_:(fun log ->
       Observe.Level.equal (Observe.Log.level log) Observe.Level.Error)
  |> Observe.Drain.with_redaction ~redaction:incident_redaction

let config =
  Observe.Config.create_exn ~service:"checkout"
    ~environment:"production"
    ~min_level:Observe.Level.Debug
    ~enrichers:[ deployment ]
    ~limits
    ~redaction:disclosure
    ~sampling
    ~retention
    ~drains:[ all_logs; incidents ]
    ()
]}

Routing sees only the safe completed log and selects one drain. Nested routes
form conjunctions. A failing route skips only its drain. Destination redaction
can strengthen the global policy but cannot recover removed source values.

The compiled [examples/production.ml] program combines these policies with two
ready filesystem drains, deliberate queue pressure, visible lifecycle loss,
flush, and shutdown.
